kosha glass

  -- amorphous solid: SiO2 + Na2O + CaO (soda-lime glass).
  -- not a crystal — no long-range order. technically a supercooled liquid.
  -- glass transition temperature Tg ≈ 550°C. below Tg: rigid. above: viscous.
  --
  -- properties:
  --   transparent: photon energy below bandgap → passes through
  --   hard (6-7 Mohs) but brittle — cracks propagate without plastic deformation
  --   coefficient of restitution: ~0.4-0.6 (shatters at high impact)
  --   thermal insulator (poor conductor: k = 1.0 W/mK)
  --   chemically inert (resists most acids except HF)
  --
  -- types: soda-lime (windows), borosilicate (Pyrex, heatproof),
  --        lead crystal (optical, high refractive index), tempered (safety).
  -- refraction index: 1.5 (standard). lead glass: 1.8+.
  --
  -- in 3d: roughness ≈ 0, metallic = 0, transparency high, refraction 1.5.

